      "patient_response": "Um... I mean, I can sit still! Mostly. I don't want you to think I'm running around the station when we're supposed to be on standby or anything. \n\nBut, I guess... well, if we're in a long meeting, or even just hanging out in the day room watching TV, I do kind of... keep moving? Like, my leg will start bouncing, or I'll be clicking a pen over and over. Sometimes I'll just keep shifting in my chair or messing with a coaster or whatever is sitting on the table in front of me. \n\nThe thing is, I don't even realize I'm doing it half the time! One of the guys will just reach over and take the pen out of my hand, and I'll be like, \"Oh, sorry!\" I'm really not trying to be disruptive or annoying, I swear. It just kind of happens when I'm trying to pay attention. That's pretty common, though, right? Like, just a way to burn off some extra energy? I hope the guys don't think I'm too distracting...",
